s":50.6,"cash_to_assets":2.6,"current_ratio":2.41,"roe":9.9,"roa":4.9,"moat":null,"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":"analysisUnavailable"},"fScore":{"score":7,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-28","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"superRobust","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-28T08:52:35.655Z","evidenceHash":"5d5cdb57f5dc34f6e7a39d125c5cd96070194ac1f43bd6a9775e6250ca31c03d"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-28","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-28T08:52:35.655Z","evidenceHash":"5d5cdb57f5dc34f6e7a39d125c5cd96070194ac1f43bd6a9775e6250ca31c03d"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/SITE.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/SITE.png","website":"https://www.siteone.com","ceo":"Doug Black","full_time_employees":"7750","description":"SiteOne Landscape Supply, Inc. operates as a leading wholesale distributor of landscaping provisions throughout the United States and Canada. The company maintains an expansive inventory of approximately 135,000 distinct stock keeping units. Its diverse product offerings encompass irrigation components, such as controllers, valves, sprinkler heads, and pipes; turf and plant care items including fertilizers, grass seeds, and ice melt; and various pest and weed control solutions like herbicides, fungicides, and rodenticides. Furthermore, SiteOne provides a wide array of landscape accessories, ranging from mulches and soil amendments to drainage pipes, tools, and sod. Their nursery department offers an extensive selection of goods, including deciduous and evergreen shrubs, ornamental and shade trees, both field-grown and container-grown stock, roses, perennials, annuals, bulbs, and other plant species. Hardscaping materials, such as pavers, natural stones, and blocks, alongside outdoor lighting products including fixtures, LED lamps, wires, and transformers, are also key parts of their catalog. Beyond products, SiteOne extends valuable consultative services, assisting clients with irrigation network design, commercial project planning, lead generation, operational support, and offers a series of technical and business management seminars. The company distributes a blend of proprietary brands, namely LESCO, SiteOne Green Tech, and Pro-Trade, alongside a variety of third-party products. Its customer base primarily consists of residential and commercial landscape professionals engaged in the design, installation, and upkeep of lawns, gardens, golf courses, and other outdoor environments, served via its branch network and direct distribution channels. As of January 2, 2022, SiteOne Landscape Supply, Inc. boasted roughly 590 branches spread across 45 U.S. states and six Canadian provinces. Established in 2013, the company's headquarters are located in Roswell, Georgia.","description_en":"SiteOne Landscape Supply, Inc. operates as a leading wholesale distributor of landscaping provisions throughout the United States and Canada. The company maintains an expansive inventory of approximately 135,000 distinct stock keeping units. Its diverse product offerings encompass irrigation components, such as controllers, valves, sprinkler heads, and pipes; turf and plant care items including fertilizers, grass seeds, and ice melt; and various pest and weed control solutions like herbicides, fungicides, and rodenticides. Furthermore, SiteOne provides a wide array of landscape accessories, ranging from mulches and soil amendments to drainage pipes, tools, and sod. Their nursery department offers an extensive selection of goods, including deciduous and evergreen shrubs, ornamental and shade trees, both field-grown and container-grown stock, roses, perennials, annuals, bulbs, and other plant species. Hardscaping materials, such as pavers, natural stones, and blocks, alongside outdoor lighting products including fixtures, LED lamps, wires, and transformers, are also key parts of their catalog. Beyond products, SiteOne extends valuable consultative services, assisting clients with irrigation network design, commercial project planning, lead generation, operational support, and offers a series of technical and business management seminars. The company distributes a blend of proprietary brands, namely LESCO, SiteOne Green Tech, and Pro-Trade, alongside a variety of third-party products. Its customer base primarily consists of residential and commercial landscape professionals engaged in the design, installation, and upkeep of lawns, gardens, golf courses, and other outdoor environments, served via its branch network and direct distribution channels. As of January 2, 2022, SiteOne Landscape Supply, Inc. boasted roughly 590 branches spread across 45 U.S. states and six Canadian provinces. Established in 2013, the company's headquarters are located in Roswell, Georgia.","description_zh":"SiteOne Landscape Supply, Inc.（美股代碼：SITE）為 Industrials 領域之重要企業，專注於 Industrial - Distribution 業務，具備清晰之商業壁壘與現金流創造能力。","address":"300 Colonial Center Parkway","city":"Roswell","state":"GA","zip":"30076","country":"US","phone":"470 277 7000","full_address":"300 Colonial Center Parkway, Roswell, GA 30076, US","range_52w":"82-168.56","year_high":168.56,"year_low":82,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":82,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-11-25","name":"Elema Eric J","title":"officer: EVP, CFO and Assistant Sec.","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":3828,"price":38.73,"total_val":0.15},{"date":"2026-11-25","name":"Elema Eric J","title":"officer: EVP, CFO and Assistant Sec.","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":2415,"price":114.4,"total_val":0.28},{"date":"2026-11-25","name":"Elema Eric J","title":"officer: EVP, CFO and Assistant Sec.","is_buy":null,"actio